aph $G$ with minimum degree at least $\\big(1-\\frac{1}{Δ+1}\\big) n$ contains every $n$-vertex graph $H$ of maximum degree at most $Δ$. Despite considerable attention, the conjecture remains widely open. We show that for bipartite $H$ this threshold can be greatly improved: there is an absolute constant $c>0$ such that every $n$-vertex graph $G$ with minimum degree at least $ \\big(1-c\\frac{\\logΔ}Δ\\big)n $ contains every $n$-vertex bipartite graph $H$ of maximum degree at most $Δ$, provided $Δ$ is not too large compared to $n$. Moreover, we prove that this logarithmic improvement is best possible up to the value of the constant. △ Less\n\nSubmitted 12 August, 2026; v1 submitted 20 July, 2026; originally announced July 2026.\n\nComments: 17 pages (small changes to the introduction)\n\n  8. arXiv:2607.03243  [pdf, ps, other] \n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn the Finiteness of the Classifying Space for Virtually Cyclic Subgroups (https://bonndoc.ulb.uni-bonn.de/xmlui/bitstream/handle/20.500.11811/7608/5151.pdf?isAllowed=y&sequence=1+)\nciteturn4search19 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.4 years ago; Crawled: 8.3 years ago; The Farrell-Jones Conjecture for Infinite Products and Minimal Families ... \\) Using fiberedness we conclude that \\(\\prod_{i\\in I} G_i\\) satisfies the FIC relative to the family \\(p_j^*(\\mathcal{F}_j)\\).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCombinatorial Calabi Flow Fundamentals (https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/combinatorial-calabi-flow)\nciteturn4search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Xu–Zheng introduce combinatorial Calabi, fractional Calabi, and $\\theta_i^{jk}$θ i jk​6-th Calabi flows with surgery under the weighted Delaunay condition ... Wu–Xu prove long-time existence and global exponential convergence of the fractional combinatorial Calabi flow for Thurston’s Euclidean and hyperbolic circle packings, and, with surgery, for 